.TH "HEAD-OBJECT"  "" "" ""
.SH NAME
head-object \- 
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
The \fBHEAD\fP operation retrieves metadata from an object without returning the object itself. This operation is useful if you\(aqre interested only in an object\(aqs metadata.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A \fBHEAD\fP request has the same options as a \fBGET\fP operation on an object. The response is identical to the \fBGET\fP response except that there is no response body. Because of this, if the \fBHEAD\fP request generates an error, it returns a generic code, such as \fB400 Bad Request\fP , \fB403 Forbidden\fP , \fB404 Not Found\fP , \fB405 Method Not Allowed\fP , \fB412 Precondition Failed\fP , or \fB304 Not Modified\fP . It\(aqs not possible to retrieve the exact exception of these error codes.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Request headers are limited to 8 KB in size. For more information, see \fI\%Common Request Headers\fP .
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Permissions
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGeneral purpose bucket permissions\fP \- To use \fBHEAD\fP , you must have the \fBs3:GetObject\fP permission. You need the relevant read object (or version) permission for this operation. For more information, see \fI\%Actions, resources, and condition keys for Amazon S3\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP . For more information about the permissions to S3 API operations by S3 resource types, see \fI\%Required permissions for Amazon S3 API operations\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP . If the object you request doesn\(aqt exist, the error that Amazon S3 returns depends on whether you also have the \fBs3:ListBucket\fP permission.
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
If you have the \fBs3:ListBucket\fP permission on the bucket, Amazon S3 returns an HTTP status code \fB404 Not Found\fP error.
.IP \(bu 2
If you don’t have the \fBs3:ListBucket\fP permission, Amazon S3 returns an HTTP status code \fB403 Forbidden\fP error.
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDirectory bucket permissions\fP \- To grant access to this API operation on a directory bucket, we recommend that you use the \(ga \fBCreateSession\fP \fI\%https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_CreateSession\fP\&.html\(ga__ API operation for session\-based authorization. Specifically, you grant the \fBs3express:CreateSession\fP permission to the directory bucket in a bucket policy or an IAM identity\-based policy. Then, you make the \fBCreateSession\fP API call on the bucket to obtain a session token. With the session token in your request header, you can make API requests to this operation. After the session token expires, you make another \fBCreateSession\fP API call to generate a new session token for use. Amazon Web Services CLI or SDKs create session and refresh the session token automatically to avoid service interruptions when a session expires. For more information about authorization, see \(ga \fBCreateSession\fP \fI\%https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_CreateSession\fP\&.html\(ga__ . If you enable \fBx\-amz\-checksum\-mode\fP in the request and the object is encrypted with Amazon Web Services Key Management Service (Amazon Web Services KMS), you must also have the \fBkms:GenerateDataKey\fP and \fBkms:Decrypt\fP permissions in IAM identity\-based policies and KMS key policies for the KMS key to retrieve the checksum of the object.
.sp
Encryption
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Encryption request headers, like \fBx\-amz\-server\-side\-encryption\fP , should not be sent for \fBHEAD\fP requests if your object uses server\-side encryption with Key Management Service (KMS) keys (SSE\-KMS), dual\-layer server\-side encryption with Amazon Web Services KMS keys (DSSE\-KMS), or server\-side encryption with Amazon S3 managed encryption keys (SSE\-S3). The \fBx\-amz\-server\-side\-encryption\fP header is used when you \fBPUT\fP an object to S3 and want to specify the encryption method. If you include this header in a \fBHEAD\fP request for an object that uses these types of keys, you’ll get an HTTP \fB400 Bad Request\fP error. It\(aqs because the encryption method can\(aqt be changed when you retrieve the object.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If you encrypt an object by using server\-side encryption with customer\-provided encryption keys (SSE\-C) when you store the object in Amazon S3, then when you retrieve the metadata from the object, you must use the following headers to provide the encryption key for the server to be able to retrieve the object\(aqs metadata. The headers are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBx\-amz\-server\-side\-encryption\-customer\-algorithm\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBx\-amz\-server\-side\-encryption\-customer\-key\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBx\-amz\-server\-side\-encryption\-customer\-key\-MD5\fP
.UNINDENT
.sp
For more information about SSE\-C, see \fI\%Server\-Side Encryption (Using Customer\-Provided Encryption Keys)\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDirectory bucket\fP \- For directory buckets, there are only two supported options for server\-side encryption: SSE\-S3 and SSE\-KMS. SSE\-C isn\(aqt supported. For more information, see \fI\%Protecting data with server\-side encryption\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Versioning
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
If the current version of the object is a delete marker, Amazon S3 behaves as if the object was deleted and includes \fBx\-amz\-delete\-marker: true\fP in the response.
.IP \(bu 2
If the specified version is a delete marker, the response returns a \fB405 Method Not Allowed\fP error and the \fBLast\-Modified: timestamp\fP response header.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- Delete marker is not supported for directory buckets.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- S3 Versioning isn\(aqt enabled and supported for directory buckets. For this API operation, only the \fBnull\fP value of the version ID is supported by directory buckets. You can only specify \fBnull\fP to the \fBversionId\fP query parameter in the request.
.UNINDENT
.sp
HTTP Host header syntax
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- The HTTP Host header syntax is \(ga\(ga \fIBucket\-name\fP .s3express\-\fIzone\-id\fP .*region\-code* .amazonaws.com\(ga\(ga .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
For directory buckets, you must make requests for this API operation to the Zonal endpoint. These endpoints support virtual\-hosted\-style requests in the format 
.nf
\(ga\(ga
.fi
\fI\%https://\fP\fIamzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket\fP .s3express\-\fIzone\-id\fP .*region\-code* .amazonaws.com/\fIkey\-name\fP \(ga\(ga . Path\-style requests are not supported. For more information about endpoints in Availability Zones, see \fI\%Regional and Zonal endpoints for directory buckets in Availability Zones\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP . For more information about endpoints in Local Zones, see \fI\%Concepts for directory buckets in Local Zones\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.IP "System Message: WARNING/2 (<string>:, line 124)"
Inline literal start\-string without end\-string.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The following actions are related to \fBHeadObject\fP :
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%GetObject\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%GetObjectAttributes\fP
.UNINDENT
.sp
See also: AWS API Documentation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
  head\-object
\-\-bucket <value>
[\-\-if\-match <value>]
[\-\-if\-modified\-since <value>]
[\-\-if\-none\-match <value>]
[\-\-if\-unmodified\-since <value>]
\-\-key <value>
[\-\-range <value>]
[\-\-response\-cache\-control <value>]
[\-\-response\-content\-disposition <value>]
[\-\-response\-content\-encoding <value>]
[\-\-response\-content\-language <value>]
[\-\-response\-content\-type <value>]
[\-\-response\-expires <value>]
[\-\-version\-id <value>]
[\-\-sse\-customer\-algorithm <value>]
[\-\-sse\-customer\-key <value>]
[\-\-sse\-customer\-key\-md5 <value>]
[\-\-request\-payer <value>]
[\-\-part\-number <value>]
[\-\-expected\-bucket\-owner <value>]
[\-\-checksum\-mode <value>]
[\-\-cli\-input\-json | \-\-cli\-input\-yaml]
[\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton <value>]
[\-\-debug]
[\-\-endpoint\-url <value>]
[\-\-no\-verify\-ssl]
[\-\-no\-paginate]
[\-\-output <value>]
[\-\-query <value>]
[\-\-profile <value>]
[\-\-region <value>]
[\-\-version <value>]
[\-\-color <value>]
[\-\-no\-sign\-request]
[\-\-ca\-bundle <value>]
[\-\-cli\-read\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-connect\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-binary\-format <value>]
[\-\-no\-cli\-pager]
[\-\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
[\-\-no\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH OPTIONS
.sp
\fB\-\-bucket\fP (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The name of the bucket that contains the object.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- When you use this operation with a directory bucket, you must use virtual\-hosted\-style requests in the format \(ga\(ga \fIBucket\-name\fP .s3express\-\fIzone\-id\fP .*region\-code* .amazonaws.com\(ga\(ga . Path\-style requests are not supported. Directory bucket names must be unique in the chosen Zone (Availability Zone or Local Zone). Bucket names must follow the format \(ga\(ga \fIbucket\-base\-name\fP \-\-\fIzone\-id\fP \-\-x\-s3\(ga\(ga (for example, \(ga\(ga \fIamzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket\fP \-\-\fIusw2\-az1\fP \-\-x\-s3\(ga\(ga ). For information about bucket naming restrictions, see \fI\%Directory bucket naming rules\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
\fBAccess points\fP \- When you use this action with an access point for general purpose buckets, you must provide the alias of the access point in place of the bucket name or specify the access point ARN. When you use this action with an access point for directory buckets, you must provide the access point name in place of the bucket name. When using the access point ARN, you must direct requests to the access point hostname. The access point hostname takes the form \fIAccessPointName\fP \-\fIAccountId\fP .s3\-accesspoint.*Region* .amazonaws.com. When using this action with an access point through the Amazon Web Services SDKs, you provide the access point ARN in place of the bucket name. For more information about access point ARNs, see \fI\%Using access points\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Object Lambda access points are not supported by directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBS3 on Outposts\fP \- When you use this action with S3 on Outposts, you must direct requests to the S3 on Outposts hostname. The S3 on Outposts hostname takes the form \(ga\(ga \fIAccessPointName\fP \-\fIAccountId\fP .*outpostID* .s3\-outposts.*Region* .amazonaws.com\(ga\(ga . When you use this action with S3 on Outposts, the destination bucket must be the Outposts access point ARN or the access point alias. For more information about S3 on Outposts, see \fI\%What is S3 on Outposts?\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-if\-match\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Return the object only if its entity tag (ETag) is the same as the one specified; otherwise, return a 412 (precondition failed) error.
.sp
If both of the \fBIf\-Match\fP and \fBIf\-Unmodified\-Since\fP headers are present in the request as follows:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIf\-Match\fP condition evaluates to \fBtrue\fP , and;
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIf\-Unmodified\-Since\fP condition evaluates to \fBfalse\fP ;
.UNINDENT
.sp
Then Amazon S3 returns \fB200 OK\fP and the data requested.
.sp
For more information about conditional requests, see \fI\%RFC 7232\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-if\-modified\-since\fP (timestamp)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Return the object only if it has been modified since the specified time; otherwise, return a 304 (not modified) error.
.sp
If both of the \fBIf\-None\-Match\fP and \fBIf\-Modified\-Since\fP headers are present in the request as follows:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIf\-None\-Match\fP condition evaluates to \fBfalse\fP , and;
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIf\-Modified\-Since\fP condition evaluates to \fBtrue\fP ;
.UNINDENT
.sp
Then Amazon S3 returns the \fB304 Not Modified\fP response code.
.sp
For more information about conditional requests, see \fI\%RFC 7232\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-if\-none\-match\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Return the object only if its entity tag (ETag) is different from the one specified; otherwise, return a 304 (not modified) error.
.sp
If both of the \fBIf\-None\-Match\fP and \fBIf\-Modified\-Since\fP headers are present in the request as follows:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIf\-None\-Match\fP condition evaluates to \fBfalse\fP , and;
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIf\-Modified\-Since\fP condition evaluates to \fBtrue\fP ;
.UNINDENT
.sp
Then Amazon S3 returns the \fB304 Not Modified\fP response code.
.sp
For more information about conditional requests, see \fI\%RFC 7232\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-if\-unmodified\-since\fP (timestamp)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Return the object only if it has not been modified since the specified time; otherwise, return a 412 (precondition failed) error.
.sp
If both of the \fBIf\-Match\fP and \fBIf\-Unmodified\-Since\fP headers are present in the request as follows:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIf\-Match\fP condition evaluates to \fBtrue\fP , and;
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIf\-Unmodified\-Since\fP condition evaluates to \fBfalse\fP ;
.UNINDENT
.sp
Then Amazon S3 returns \fB200 OK\fP and the data requested.
.sp
For more information about conditional requests, see \fI\%RFC 7232\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-key\fP (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The object key.
.sp
Constraints:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
min: \fB1\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-range\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
HeadObject returns only the metadata for an object. If the Range is satisfiable, only the \fBContentLength\fP is affected in the response. If the Range is not satisfiable, S3 returns a \fB416 \- Requested Range Not Satisfiable\fP error.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-response\-cache\-control\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Sets the \fBCache\-Control\fP header of the response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-response\-content\-disposition\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Sets the \fBContent\-Disposition\fP header of the response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-response\-content\-encoding\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Sets the \fBContent\-Encoding\fP header of the response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-response\-content\-language\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Sets the \fBContent\-Language\fP header of the response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-response\-content\-type\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Sets the \fBContent\-Type\fP header of the response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-response\-expires\fP (timestamp)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Sets the \fBExpires\fP header of the response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-version\-id\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Version ID used to reference a specific version of the object.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
For directory buckets in this API operation, only the \fBnull\fP value of the version ID is supported.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-sse\-customer\-algorithm\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the algorithm to use when encrypting the object (for example, AES256).
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-sse\-customer\-key\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the customer\-provided encryption key for Amazon S3 to use in encrypting data. This value is used to store the object and then it is discarded; Amazon S3 does not store the encryption key. The key must be appropriate for use with the algorithm specified in the \fBx\-amz\-server\-side\-encryption\-customer\-algorithm\fP header.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-sse\-customer\-key\-md5\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the 128\-bit MD5 digest of the encryption key according to RFC 1321. Amazon S3 uses this header for a message integrity check to ensure that the encryption key was transmitted without error.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-request\-payer\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Confirms that the requester knows that they will be charged for the request. Bucket owners need not specify this parameter in their requests. If either the source or destination S3 bucket has Requester Pays enabled, the requester will pay for corresponding charges to copy the object. For information about downloading objects from Requester Pays buckets, see \fI\%Downloading Objects in Requester Pays Buckets\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrequester\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-part\-number\fP (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Part number of the object being read. This is a positive integer between 1 and 10,000. Effectively performs a \(aqranged\(aq HEAD request for the part specified. Useful querying about the size of the part and the number of parts in this object.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-expected\-bucket\-owner\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The account ID of the expected bucket owner. If the account ID that you provide does not match the actual owner of the bucket, the request fails with the HTTP status code \fB403 Forbidden\fP (access denied).
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-checksum\-mode\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
To retrieve the checksum, this parameter must be enabled.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBGeneral purpose buckets\fP \- If you enable checksum mode and the object is uploaded with a \fI\%checksum\fP and encrypted with an Key Management Service (KMS) key, you must have permission to use the \fBkms:Decrypt\fP action to retrieve the checksum.
.sp
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- If you enable \fBChecksumMode\fP and the object is encrypted with Amazon Web Services Key Management Service (Amazon Web Services KMS), you must also have the \fBkms:GenerateDataKey\fP and \fBkms:Decrypt\fP permissions in IAM identity\-based policies and KMS key policies for the KMS key to retrieve the checksum of the object.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBENABLED\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-input\-json\fP | \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP (string)
Reads arguments from the JSON string provided. The JSON string follows the format provided by \fB\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton\fP\&. If other arguments are provided on the command line, those values will override the JSON\-provided values. It is not possible to pass arbitrary binary values using a JSON\-provided value as the string will be taken literally. This may not be specified along with \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP\&.
.sp
\fB\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton\fP (string)
Prints a JSON skeleton to standard output without sending an API request. If provided with no value or the value \fBinput\fP, prints a sample input JSON that can be used as an argument for \fB\-\-cli\-input\-json\fP\&. Similarly, if provided \fByaml\-input\fP it will print a sample input YAML that can be used with \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP\&. If provided with the value \fBoutput\fP, it validates the command inputs and returns a sample output JSON for that command. The generated JSON skeleton is not stable between versions of the AWS CLI and there are no backwards compatibility guarantees in the JSON skeleton generated.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.sp
\fB\-\-debug\fP (boolean)
.sp
Turn on debug logging.
.sp
\fB\-\-endpoint\-url\fP (string)
.sp
Override command\(aqs default URL with the given URL.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-verify\-ssl\fP (boolean)
.sp
By default, the AWS CLI uses SSL when communicating with AWS services. For each SSL connection, the AWS CLI will verify SSL certificates. This option overrides the default behavior of verifying SSL certificates.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-paginate\fP (boolean)
.sp
Disable automatic pagination. If automatic pagination is disabled, the AWS CLI will only make one call, for the first page of results.
.sp
\fB\-\-output\fP (string)
.sp
The formatting style for command output.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
text
.IP \(bu 2
table
.IP \(bu 2
yaml
.IP \(bu 2
yaml\-stream
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-query\fP (string)
.sp
A JMESPath query to use in filtering the response data.
.sp
\fB\-\-profile\fP (string)
.sp
Use a specific profile from your credential file.
.sp
\fB\-\-region\fP (string)
.sp
The region to use. Overrides config/env settings.
.sp
\fB\-\-version\fP (string)
.sp
Display the version of this tool.
.sp
\fB\-\-color\fP (string)
.sp
Turn on/off color output.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-sign\-request\fP (boolean)
.sp
Do not sign requests. Credentials will not be loaded if this argument is provided.
.sp
\fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fP (string)
.sp
The CA certificate bundle to use when verifying SSL certificates. Overrides config/env settings.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-read\-timeout\fP (int)
.sp
The maximum socket read time in seconds. If the value is set to 0, the socket read will be blocking and not timeout. The default value is 60 seconds.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-connect\-timeout\fP (int)
.sp
The maximum socket connect time in seconds. If the value is set to 0, the socket connect will be blocking and not timeout. The default value is 60 seconds.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-binary\-format\fP (string)
.sp
The formatting style to be used for binary blobs. The default format is base64. The base64 format expects binary blobs to be provided as a base64 encoded string. The raw\-in\-base64\-out format preserves compatibility with AWS CLI V1 behavior and binary values must be passed literally. When providing contents from a file that map to a binary blob \fBfileb://\fP will always be treated as binary and use the file contents directly regardless of the \fBcli\-binary\-format\fP setting. When using \fBfile://\fP the file contents will need to properly formatted for the configured \fBcli\-binary\-format\fP\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
base64
.IP \(bu 2
raw\-in\-base64\-out
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-cli\-pager\fP (boolean)
.sp
Disable cli pager for output.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-auto\-prompt\fP (boolean)
.sp
Automatically prompt for CLI input parameters.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-cli\-auto\-prompt\fP (boolean)
.sp
Disable automatically prompt for CLI input parameters.
.SH EXAMPLES
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
To use the following examples, you must have the AWS CLI installed and configured. See the \fI\%Getting started guide\fP in the \fIAWS CLI User Guide\fP for more information.
.sp
Unless otherwise stated, all examples have unix\-like quotation rules. These examples will need to be adapted to your terminal\(aqs quoting rules. See \fI\%Using quotation marks with strings\fP in the \fIAWS CLI User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The following command retrieves metadata for an object in a bucket named \fBamzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3api head\-object \-\-bucket amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket \-\-key index.html
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Output:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
{
    \(dqAcceptRanges\(dq: \(dqbytes\(dq,
    \(dqContentType\(dq: \(dqtext/html\(dq,
    \(dqLastModified\(dq: \(dqThu, 16 Apr 2015 18:19:14 GMT\(dq,
    \(dqContentLength\(dq: 77,
    \(dqVersionId\(dq: \(dqnull\(dq,
    \(dqETag\(dq: \(dq\e\(dq30a6ec7e1a9ad79c203d05a589c8b400\e\(dq\(dq,
    \(dqMetadata\(dq: {}
}
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH OUTPUT
.sp
DeleteMarker \-> (boolean)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies whether the object retrieved was (true) or was not (false) a Delete Marker. If false, this response header does not appear in the response.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
AcceptRanges \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Indicates that a range of bytes was specified.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Expiration \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If the object expiration is configured (see \(ga \fBPutBucketLifecycleConfiguration\fP \fI\%https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_PutBucketLifecycleConfiguration\fP\&.html\(ga__ ), the response includes this header. It includes the \fBexpiry\-date\fP and \fBrule\-id\fP key\-value pairs providing object expiration information. The value of the \fBrule\-id\fP is URL\-encoded.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Object expiration information is not returned in directory buckets and this header returns the value \(dq\fBNotImplemented\fP \(dq in all responses for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Restore \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If the object is an archived object (an object whose storage class is GLACIER), the response includes this header if either the archive restoration is in progress (see \fI\%RestoreObject\fP or an archive copy is already restored.
.sp
If an archive copy is already restored, the header value indicates when Amazon S3 is scheduled to delete the object copy. For example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBx\-amz\-restore: ongoing\-request=\(dqfalse\(dq, expiry\-date=\(dqFri, 21 Dec 2012 00:00:00 GMT\(dq\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If the object restoration is in progress, the header returns the value \fBongoing\-request=\(dqtrue\(dq\fP .
.sp
For more information about archiving objects, see \fI\%Transitioning Objects: General Considerations\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets. Directory buckets only support \fBEXPRESS_ONEZONE\fP (the S3 Express One Zone storage class) in Availability Zones and \fBONEZONE_IA\fP (the S3 One Zone\-Infrequent Access storage class) in Dedicated Local Zones.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ArchiveStatus \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The archive state of the head object.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBARCHIVE_ACCESS\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDEEP_ARCHIVE_ACCESS\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
LastModified \-> (timestamp)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Date and time when the object was last modified.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ContentLength \-> (long)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Size of the body in bytes.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumCRC32 \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Base64 encoded, 32\-bit \fBCRC32 checksum\fP of the object. This checksum is only be present if the checksum was uploaded with the object. When you use an API operation on an object that was uploaded using multipart uploads, this value may not be a direct checksum value of the full object. Instead, it\(aqs a calculation based on the checksum values of each individual part. For more information about how checksums are calculated with multipart uploads, see \fI\%Checking object integrity\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumCRC32C \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Base64 encoded, 32\-bit \fBCRC32C\fP checksum of the object. This checksum is only present if the checksum was uploaded with the object. When you use an API operation on an object that was uploaded using multipart uploads, this value may not be a direct checksum value of the full object. Instead, it\(aqs a calculation based on the checksum values of each individual part. For more information about how checksums are calculated with multipart uploads, see \fI\%Checking object integrity\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumCRC64NVME \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Base64 encoded, 64\-bit \fBCRC64NVME\fP checksum of the object. For more information, see \fI\%Checking object integrity in the Amazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumSHA1 \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Base64 encoded, 160\-bit \fBSHA1\fP digest of the object. This will only be present if the object was uploaded with the object. When you use the API operation on an object that was uploaded using multipart uploads, this value may not be a direct checksum value of the full object. Instead, it\(aqs a calculation based on the checksum values of each individual part. For more information about how checksums are calculated with multipart uploads, see \fI\%Checking object integrity\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumSHA256 \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Base64 encoded, 256\-bit \fBSHA256\fP digest of the object. This will only be present if the object was uploaded with the object. When you use an API operation on an object that was uploaded using multipart uploads, this value may not be a direct checksum value of the full object. Instead, it\(aqs a calculation based on the checksum values of each individual part. For more information about how checksums are calculated with multipart uploads, see \fI\%Checking object integrity\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumType \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The checksum type, which determines how part\-level checksums are combined to create an object\-level checksum for multipart objects. You can use this header response to verify that the checksum type that is received is the same checksum type that was specified in \fBCreateMultipartUpload\fP request. For more information, see \fI\%Checking object integrity in the Amazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCOMPOSITE\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFULL_OBJECT\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ETag \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
An entity tag (ETag) is an opaque identifier assigned by a web server to a specific version of a resource found at a URL.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
MissingMeta \-> (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This is set to the number of metadata entries not returned in \fBx\-amz\-meta\fP headers. This can happen if you create metadata using an API like SOAP that supports more flexible metadata than the REST API. For example, using SOAP, you can create metadata whose values are not legal HTTP headers.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
VersionId \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Version ID of the object.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
CacheControl \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies caching behavior along the request/reply chain.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ContentDisposition \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies presentational information for the object.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ContentEncoding \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Indicates what content encodings have been applied to the object and thus what decoding mechanisms must be applied to obtain the media\-type referenced by the Content\-Type header field.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ContentLanguage \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The language the content is in.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ContentType \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A standard MIME type describing the format of the object data.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ContentRange \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The portion of the object returned in the response for a \fBGET\fP request.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Expires \-> (timestamp)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The date and time at which the object is no longer cacheable.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This member has been deprecated. Please use \fIExpiresString\fP instead.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ExpiresString \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The raw, unparsed value of the \fBExpires\fP field.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
WebsiteRedirectLocation \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If the bucket is configured as a website, redirects requests for this object to another object in the same bucket or to an external URL. Amazon S3 stores the value of this header in the object metadata.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ServerSideEncryption \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The server\-side encryption algorithm used when you store this object in Amazon S3 or Amazon FSx.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
When accessing data stored in Amazon FSx file systems using S3 access points, the only valid server side encryption option is \fBaws:fsx\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAES256\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBaws:fsx\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBaws:kms\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBaws:kms:dsse\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Metadata \-> (map)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A map of metadata to store with the object in S3.
.sp
key \-> (string)
.sp
value \-> (string)
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
SSECustomerAlgorithm \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If server\-side encryption with a customer\-provided encryption key was requested, the response will include this header to confirm the encryption algorithm that\(aqs used.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
SSECustomerKeyMD5 \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If server\-side encryption with a customer\-provided encryption key was requested, the response will include this header to provide the round\-trip message integrity verification of the customer\-provided encryption key.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
SSEKMSKeyId \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If present, indicates the ID of the KMS key that was used for object encryption.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
BucketKeyEnabled \-> (boolean)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Indicates whether the object uses an S3 Bucket Key for server\-side encryption with Key Management Service (KMS) keys (SSE\-KMS).
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
StorageClass \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Provides storage class information of the object. Amazon S3 returns this header for all objects except for S3 Standard storage class objects.
.sp
For more information, see \fI\%Storage Classes\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- Directory buckets only support \fBEXPRESS_ONEZONE\fP (the S3 Express One Zone storage class) in Availability Zones and \fBONEZONE_IA\fP (the S3 One Zone\-Infrequent Access storage class) in Dedicated Local Zones.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSTANDARD\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBREDUCED_REDUNDANCY\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSTANDARD_IA\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBONEZONE_IA\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBINTELLIGENT_TIERING\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGLACIER\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDEEP_ARCHIVE\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOUTPOSTS\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGLACIER_IR\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSNOW\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEXPRESS_ONEZONE\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFSX_OPENZFS\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
RequestCharged \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If present, indicates that the requester was successfully charged for the request. For more information, see \fI\%Using Requester Pays buckets for storage transfers and usage\fP in the \fIAmazon Simple Storage Service user guide\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrequester\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ReplicationStatus \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Amazon S3 can return this header if your request involves a bucket that is either a source or a destination in a replication rule.
.sp
In replication, you have a source bucket on which you configure replication and destination bucket or buckets where Amazon S3 stores object replicas. When you request an object (\fBGetObject\fP ) or object metadata (\fBHeadObject\fP ) from these buckets, Amazon S3 will return the \fBx\-amz\-replication\-status\fP header in the response as follows:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIf requesting an object from the source bucket\fP , Amazon S3 will return the \fBx\-amz\-replication\-status\fP header if the object in your request is eligible for replication. For example, suppose that in your replication configuration, you specify object prefix \fBTaxDocs\fP requesting Amazon S3 to replicate objects with key prefix \fBTaxDocs\fP . Any objects you upload with this key name prefix, for example \fBTaxDocs/document1.pdf\fP , are eligible for replication. For any object request with this key name prefix, Amazon S3 will return the \fBx\-amz\-replication\-status\fP header with value PENDING, COMPLETED or FAILED indicating object replication status.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIf requesting an object from a destination bucket\fP , Amazon S3 will return the \fBx\-amz\-replication\-status\fP header with value REPLICA if the object in your request is a replica that Amazon S3 created and there is no replica modification replication in progress.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWhen replicating objects to multiple destination buckets\fP , the \fBx\-amz\-replication\-status\fP header acts differently. The header of the source object will only return a value of COMPLETED when replication is successful to all destinations. The header will remain at value PENDING until replication has completed for all destinations. If one or more destinations fails replication the header will return FAILED.
.UNINDENT
.sp
For more information, see \fI\%Replication\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCOMPLETE\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPENDING\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFAILED\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBREPLICA\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCOMPLETED\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
PartsCount \-> (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The count of parts this object has. This value is only returned if you specify \fBpartNumber\fP in your request and the object was uploaded as a multipart upload.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
TagCount \-> (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The number of tags, if any, on the object, when you have the relevant permission to read object tags.
.sp
You can use \fI\%GetObjectTagging\fP to retrieve the tag set associated with an object.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ObjectLockMode \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Object Lock mode, if any, that\(aqs in effect for this object. This header is only returned if the requester has the \fBs3:GetObjectRetention\fP permission. For more information about S3 Object Lock, see \fI\%Object Lock\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGOVERNANCE\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCOMPLIANCE\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ObjectLockRetainUntilDate \-> (timestamp)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The date and time when the Object Lock retention period expires. This header is only returned if the requester has the \fBs3:GetObjectRetention\fP permission.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ObjectLockLegalHoldStatus \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies whether a legal hold is in effect for this object. This header is only returned if the requester has the \fBs3:GetObjectLegalHold\fP permission. This header is not returned if the specified version of this object has never had a legal hold applied. For more information about S3 Object Lock, see \fI\%Object Lock\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBON\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOFF\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
